#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we walk through the four steps of the Qiskit pattern on a "
"seven-qubit instance of the labeling-cosets-with-error problem and evaluate "
"a single kernel matrix entry using the `StatevectorSampler` primitive from "
"Qiskit. A statevector simulator is exact (up to shot noise) and shows us the"
" method end-to-end without consuming QPU time. We then repeat the same "
"instance on real hardware in the hardware example section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa seksyong ito, tatalakay tayo sa apat na hakbang ng Qiskit pattern sa "
"isang pitong-qubit na instance ng labeling-cosets-with-error problem at "
"suriin ang isang kernel matrix entry gamit ang `StatevectorSampler` "
"primitive mula sa Qiskit. Ang statevector simulator ay eksakto (hanggang sa "
"shot noise) at ipinapakita sa atin ang paraan mula simula hanggang katapusan"
" nang hindi gumagamit ng QPU time. Uulitin natin ang parehong instance sa "
"tunay na hardware sa seksyon ng hardware example.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input: Training dataset.\n"
msgstr "Input: Training dataset.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Output: Abstract circuit for calculating a kernel matrix entry.\n"
msgstr "Output: Abstract circuit para sa pagkalkula ng kernel matrix entry.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The binary classification problem we aim to solve here is referred to as \"[_labeling cosets with error_](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.03406).\" The input training dataset contains a group structure, consisting of two cosets formed by a group and subgroup.\n"
"The group is taken to be $G = SU(2)^{\\otimes n}$ for qubits, which is the special unitary group of\n"
"$2 \\times 2$ matrices and has wide applicability in nature; e.g., the Standard Model of particle physics.\n"
"We take the (graph-stabilizer) subgroup $S_\\text{graph} < G$ with $S_\\text{graph} = \\langle \\{ X_i \\otimes _{k:(k,i) \\in \\mathcal{E}} Z_k\\} _{i \\in \\mathcal{V}} \\} \\rangle$ for a graph with edges $\\mathcal{E}$ and vertices $\\mathcal{V}$.\n"
"Note that the stabilizers fix a stabilizer state such that $D_s | \\psi \\rangle = | \\psi \\rangle,~ \\forall s \\in S_\\text{graph}$.\n"
"Finally, we define two left-cosets $C_\\pm = c_\\pm S_\\text{graph}$ by drawing two $c_\\pm \\in G$ at random.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang binary classification problem na layunin nating lutasin dito ay tinatawag na \"[_labeling cosets with error_](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.03406).\" Ang input training dataset ay naglalaman ng group structure, na binubuo ng dalawang coset na nabuo ng isang grupo at subgroup.\n"
"Ang grupo ay kinuha bilang $G = SU(2)^{\\otimes n}$ para sa mga qubit, na siyang espesyal na unitary group ng\n"
"$2 \\times 2$ matrices at may malawak na pagiging angkop sa kalikasan; hal., ang Standard Model ng particle physics.\n"
"Kinukuha natin ang (graph-stabilizer) subgroup na $S_\\text{graph} < G$ na may $S_\\text{graph} = \\langle \\{ X_i \\otimes _{k:(k,i) \\in \\mathcal{E}} Z_k\\} _{i \\in \\mathcal{V}} \\} \\rangle$ para sa isang graph na may mga gilid na $\\mathcal{E}$ at mga vertex na $\\mathcal{V}$.\n"
"Tandaan na ang mga stabilizer ay nag-aayos ng stabilizer state upang ang $D_s | \\psi \\rangle = | \\psi \\rangle,~ \\forall s \\in S_\\text{graph}$.\n"
"Sa wakas, nagtatakda tayo ng dalawang left-coset na $C_\\pm = c_\\pm S_\\text{graph}$ sa pamamagitan ng pagkuha ng dalawang $c_\\pm \\in G$ nang random.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more details about the dataset and how it is generated, see [this "
"notebook](https://github.com/qiskit-community/prototype-quantum-kernel-"
